asciicam (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
  * Add a neural speech-to-text engine (asrnet): --model <weights>
    with --listen now transcribes full sentences from a real neural
    model instead of matching enrolled word templates (weights are a
    plain safetensors file; vocabulary from tokenizer.json beside it).
  * Add --mic <device>: capture audio straight from an ALSA microphone
    for --listen, instead of only a file, fifo or stdin.
  * Add --asr-debug: with --model, print the decoder's raw and
    repeat-trimmed token ids to stderr, for diagnosing transcription
    issues.
  * Fix a repeated short word or phrase (e.g. "hi, hi, hi.") being
    over-trimmed to two repeats; genuinely repeated short speech is now
    kept, while the decoder getting stuck in a loop is still cut.
  * Performance: the neural network's matrix-multiply picks an AVX2
    implementation at runtime on CPUs that support it, falling back to
    the portable SSE path elsewhere.

 -- Harshit Dhanwalkar <harshitpd1729@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:27:00 +0530
